invariant: INV-17
file: src/ghash_hw.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: gcm_powers_hw does not wipe the ghash_state it computed the eight
  powers in, so the hash subkey and its powers stay on the stack below
  each call that keys an AES-GCM direction. Every stored byte is right.
  bin/aes_suite_test copies the stack below gcm_traffic_key_store and
  requires no round key, no hash subkey and no power there
  (test/ghash_powers_tests.h, docs/decisions.md 234).

--- old
    // s holds the subkey, the eight powers and the last product's sums.
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    // s holds the subkey, the eight powers and the last product's sums.
